[agent:result]         start_time:
[agent:result]             Inclusive lower bound on the `event_time` column (`event_time >= start_time`).
[agent:result]             If not provided and `wallclock_time` is also not set, defaults to the
[agent:result]             `HOPS_START_TIME` environment variable when set (scheduler-supplied
[agent:result]             data-interval start). When `wallclock_time` is set the env-var fallback is
[agent:result]             skipped — wallclock_time takes precedence. An explicit `start_time` always
[agent:result]             wins over both. If neither `start_time` nor `HOPS_START_TIME` is set, no
[agent:result]             lower bound is applied (the whole feature group is read).
[agent:result]             Can be a `datetime`, `date`, Unix timestamp (int), pandas `Timestamp`, or a string formatted as
[agent:result]             `%Y-%m-%d`, `%Y-%m-%d %H`, `%Y-%m-%d %H:%M`, `%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S`, `%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S.%f`,
